{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 3) ∨ (ndim(v_2) > 3) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) < 1000) ∧ (∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1]: shape(v_2, j) < 1000)
>>
Rule 100 (Dtype of the tensor must be integer or floating or complex and if it is floating or complex then it's value cannot be nan, inf or -inf)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ((2 <= dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) <= 10) ∧ (2 <= dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) <= 10)) ∧ if ((6 <= dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) <= 8) ∨ (9 <= dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) <= 10) ∨ (6 <= dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) <= 8) ∨ (9 <= dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) <= 10)) then ((∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, i) - 1] : v_1[j] ≠ "NaN" ∧ v_1[j] ≠ "inf" ∧ v_1[j] ≠ "-inf") ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_2, i) - 1] : v_2[j] ≠ "NaN" ∧ v_2[j] ≠ "inf" ∧ v_2[j] ≠ "-inf"))
>>
Rule 102 (If input tensors has dimensions greater than 0, then each dimension must be greater than 0.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1)-1]: shape(v_1, i) > 0) ∧ (∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2)-1]: shape(v_2, j) > 0)
>>
Rule 103 (If one input is a scalar tensor, then the other should have a numerical datatype.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then (2 <= dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) <= 10) else if ndim(v_2) = 0 then (2 <= dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) <= 10)
>>
Rule 105 (Each input tensor element should be finite.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1)-1]: ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, i)-1]: v_1[j] ≠ "inf" ∧ v_1[j] ≠ "-inf" ∧ v_1[j] ≠ "NaN") ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2)-1]: ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_2, i)-1]: v_2[j] ≠ "inf" ∧ v_2[j] ≠ "-inf" ∧ v_2[j] ≠ "NaN")
